    "result_text": "That's just JaCoCo coverage excludes, not test excludes. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the whole build.\n\nThe change is complete and green. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipTier` is a **derived, read-time field** computed in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`. I added the GOLD rule while preserving the existing BRONZE/SILVER logic.\n\n**New file \u2014 `MembershipTier.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`): centralizes the tier logic with clear precedence:\n- **GOLD** \u2014 owner has a `householdId` and 3+ owners share it (counted via `OwnerRepository`, matching how `AssignHousehold` stamps household members at create time).\n- **SILVER** \u2014 unique name (`namesakeCount == 0`) and an email on file (unchanged rule).\n- **BRONZE** \u2014 otherwise.\n\nI compute at read time rather than persisting, so every member of a household that crosses the threshold reports GOLD \u2014 including members created before the third one joined.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**: converted from an interface to an abstract class so the mapping expression can consult an `@Autowired OwnerRepository` (an owner's own fields can't reveal household size). The `membershipTier` expression now delegates to `MembershipTier.of(owner, ownerRepository)`. Because the change lives in the mapper, it applies uniformly to every read path (single GET, list, page), not just the one the test exercises.\n\n**Verification**: the new `AcceptanceTest.coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` passes (third member of a shared household is GOLD), and the full `mvnw test` build is green. I confirmed the generated `OwnerMapperImpl` extends the abstract mapper and correctly uses the injected repository.\n\nOne note: this counts household size with `ownerRepository.findAll()` at read time (consistent with existing functions like `AssignNamesakeCount`), which is fine for this sample app's scale but would warrant a targeted count query if the owner table grew large.",
